    "summary": "merge-bot slot never re-arms after externally-merged PR (fa #1563 queued 3h with green checks)",
    "description": "Live 2026-10-17 07:00–08:10Z, IstiN/flutter_agent_harness:\n\n1. PR #1661 was merged by the OWNER via bypass at 06:30Z while the machine had armed its validation (Quality gate / Binaries smoke pending stamps at 06:04Z). The machine's merge path never ran for it.\n2. Since then the merge bot logs all 7 approved PRs as `⏳ FIFO-queued (awaiting validate-armed turn)` and arms NOBODY (acted: 0) — the validation slot appears permanently held/absent.\n3. Queue head #1563: approved, ai_pr_reviewed, 0 commits behind main, every check green — but BLOCKED (no Quality gate stamp on current head) and carrying a stale `validation_failed` label from an older head. Four+ SM ticks since: never re-armed.\nExpected: (a) the slot bookkeeping must detect the slot-holder PR is MERGED (or the armed stamps belong to a merged PR) and release; (b) a PR whose head moved after `validation_failed` must get validation re-armed on the fresh head (stale-label cleanup). Workaround used meanwhile: none — human nudge required. Related: #944 (latch/twin-guard family, fixed by #945)."
  }
