====================================================================================================
RULE 11 : Every open non-draft PR behind main gets a silent branch refresh with the workflow token (pushes trigger no workflows, so freshness is free); validating PRs are excluded so the validation head never moves mid-run. mergeState is BEHIND only: the prStatus deterministic override computes BEHIND from base freshness (immune to the REST BEHIND/BLOCKED flip-flop this rule used to paper over with both values), and BLOCKED is now a REAL verdict (fresh head, required checks pending/red) — updating those would no-op-clone every pending PR on every tick. Limit 20 (owner 2026-09-22): silent pushes fire no CI — refreshing every BEHIND head every tick is free and keeps PRs merge-ready, so the merge window never waits for a refresh first. STICKY PARK (owner 2026-09-27, live: fa#923): before refreshing, a GUEST PR whose current head has RED checks is labeled validation_failed (idempotent, the head SHA noted in a one-time comment) — validate-armed excludes the label and no validation CI is dispatched for it at all; the label is REMOVED only when the LAST SUBSTANTIVE commit (machine-authored merges of main walked back past, dmtools-agents#681) is a NON-machine push NEWER than the park, so the SM's own silent-updates — bot merges or re-arms — never clear a red guest's park. Machine-authored PRs never get the label (fa pushes their heads; the label's SET rules are guest-gated — legacy parks predate that). MACHINE SELF-CLEAR (gh-750, owner directive 2026-10-05): a MACHINE-authored parked PR — legacy residue like fa#1227, the label predates this guest-only contract — clears when the current head's check rollup is GREEN or the head moved past the park carrying no red verdict of its own (probe failures keep the park, fail closed); guests keep the 2026-09-27 sticky behavior.
