The fixture serves a SINGLE PR via github_list_prs (`[{number: pr.number}]`) and always the same body from github_get_pr. For my gh-952 tests I need multi-PR scenarios + a merged-PR list. The fixture's `github_list_prs` ignores args — I need a state-aware variant. I'll extend the fixture minimally: support `opts.openPrs` (a list of {number} refs) and `opts.prByNumber` (number → PR body) and `opts.mergedPrs` (raw REST list payload), while keeping all existing tests untouched. Actually — cleaner: add support WITHOUT touching existing behavior:
- `github_list_prs: function (a)` — if `opts.prIndex` (a map from state→list of PR bodies) is provided, serve `a.state` from it (default 'open'); else fall back today's single-PR behavior.

The bot fetches each open PR by number via github_get_pr — with prIndex I need per-number bodies: serve from a map.

Let me design the new tests:

```js
suite('mergeBot: externally-merged slot holder releases the merge window (gh-952)', function () {
    // Live fa 2026-10-17 07:00–08:10Z: PR #1661 was merged by the OWNER via
    // bypass while its validation was armed (pending Quality gate stamps).
    // The machine's merge path never ran; the open list then shows NO armed
    // PR, every approved PR defers as 'FIFO-queued (awaiting validate-armed
    // turn)', acted: 0 — the slot looks permanently held/absent and the
    // queue starves behind a holder that will NEVER validate again.

    test('recently-merged armed holder → slot released: a validated candidate advances, release is logged', ...)
    test('merged holder beyond the recency window → stale archaeology, no release', ...)
    test('merged PR without the merge-window arm → not a holder, ignored', ...)
    test('no validated candidate → release still logged, deferrals continue, self-tick fires', ...)
    test('open armed holder still present → no merged probe, no release line', ...)
});
```

